      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T11:15:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me identify the problem here. Once `_kvm_host_prot_finalize` is done, we start trapping on the ITS/GICR registers.\n\nWe cannot initialize the ITS/GICR emulation structures before `_kvm_host_prot_finalize` because there is a time window when structures could disconnect from hw state (host making last second changes after structures were made). For this reason we currently lock in `(its|gic)_start_deprivilage`. \n\nIf we would try to initialize the structures after `_kvm_host_prot_finalize`. We would create a time window when the ITS/GICR are trapped, but the structures to handle an emulation are not there yet. Also there would be a short moment when trapping could happen during initialization of said structures.\n\nSo I suggest the following:\n\n* Get rid of `(its|gic)_start_deprivilage` (merge it with `(its|gic)_end_deprivilage`, rename it etc)\n* after `_kvm_host_prot_finalize` the `reg-\u003epriv` would be still `NULL` so basically we would forward all access through `pkvm_handle_forward_req` until all are initialized.\n* We go over each ITS/GICR one by one and initialize them (lock, hvc, `reg-\u003epriv \u003d ...`, unlock)\n* Once everything is initialized we no longer allow forwarding if `reg-\u003epriv` is `NULL`\n\nThere could be a problem if host would change the HW state without holding the lock when the emulation structure would be initialized. However this should not happen.\n\nThat said I am not sure what is to gain apart from more granular locking (which is indeed a good argument on it\u0027s own). And I agree it would be more suited for upstream. \n\nHowever in Android case I don\u0027t expect any devices to be configured around the `_kvm_host_prot_finalize` call. All drivers of the devices issuing MSIs should be deferred until IOMMU protected driver is loaded, which happens at a later stage.\n\nPlease let me know WDYT about above proposal. (Btw thanks for the review!)",
      "parentUuid": "f91893c7_46f6f4c6",
      "revId": "08db0287b1cda8650414a245e5a64d5fd302e468",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2c7adcb_9cc63b90",
        "filename": "drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c",
