      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T12:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure I follow the suggestion but dropping registers access as mentioned in \n```\nDropping instead (what pkvm_handle_gic_emulation and pkvm_handle_rdist_emulation already do when priv is NULL) keeps HW frozen across the snapshot, so the invariant holds.\n```\nis a bad ideea. \n\nThe only thing that we should care here is avoiding a watchdog that can fire while we stay for too long at EL2 and this is why doing it per/node granular locking is beneficial. Since in most of the cases we only have max two ITS nodes I won\u0027t be too worried about that.",
      "parentUuid": "fb1ab6c6_f49546b7",
      "revId": "08db0287b1cda8650414a245e5a64d5fd302e468",
